  "body": "The contributor's request (#662): Open and Model offer the last few projects and models, so a re-open is one click.\n\n## What changed\n- **`camcraft_app::recent`** holds two lists, projects and models:\n  - newest first, de-duplicated by canonical path;\n  - cap N = 10, read from the file's `limit` key (0 turns it off; capped at 50);\n  - the write is atomic and reuses `machine::store::write_atomic`.\n- **Storage:** `<config>/camcraft/recent.json`, tagged `camcraft-recent/1`.\n  - `<config>` is `%APPDATA%` on Windows, `~/Library/Application Support` on macOS, and `$XDG_CONFIG_HOME` or `~/.config` on Linux. `CAMCRAFT_CONFIG_DIR` overrides it.\n  - **No new dependency.**\n- **Bad files:** a corrupt, unreadable or wrong-format file starts empty, with a logged warning and a status line. A file that doesn't exist yet starts empty quietly.\n- **When an entry is added:** after a successful project open or save (Save and Save As), and after a model import that lands. A failed open adds nothing.\n- **Commands:** `CommandKind::OpenRecent` and `ClearRecent`.\n  - `OpenRecent` runs the same open and import paths as the dialogs, and a project takes the same unsaved-changes prompt as Open.\n  - A missing file is refused by name at click time and again when the command runs.\n  - The lists are preference state, so they stay off the undo history.\n- **UI:** the toolbar's **Open** and **Model** drop down a list when it has entries:\n  - each file name, with the full path on hover;\n  - a missing file greyed as \"name (missing)\";\n  - **Clear recent** and **Browse…** at the bottom.\n  - Every row has an AccessKit label. With an empty list or the feature off, the button opens the dialog as before, and Ctrl+O / Ctrl+Shift+O still open the dialogs directly.\n- **Recorded in `docs/decisions/662-recent-files.md`:** there's no Settings UI yet, so the cap is a config key, and there's no File menu since the imgui shell went, so there's no \"Open Recent\" submenu.\n- **Test isolation:** only the real window reads or writes the per-user file, so test suites never touch the user's recents.\n\n## How tested\n- **App `recent_files` (11):**\n  - add and newest-first;\n  - canonical de-dup;\n  - cap, a smaller cap, and 0;\n  - clear;\n  - missing files;\n  - a restart round-trip (no `.tmp` left behind);\n  - no file yet;\n  - corrupt, wrong-format, wrong-types and unreadable files;\n  - hand-edit clean-up;\n  - the per-platform folder and its override.\n- **UI `recent_door` (8, egui_kittest with real clicks):**\n  - the AccessKit row structure;\n  - Save fills the list, and an entry opens through Open;\n  - the unsaved prompt, then Don't Save, opens it;\n  - a missing entry is refused by name;\n  - Clear recent;\n  - a recent model imports and moves to the top;\n  - an empty list and Browse… open today's dialog;\n  - restart and a corrupt file.\n- **Gate:**\n  - ui lib 384 pass. The 1 failure is `headless_run_succeeds` (no GPU adapter in the agent sandbox), which fails the same on clean main;\n  - project_roundtrip 69, commands_undo 32 and machine_edit 12 pass;\n  - clippy is clean. No snapshot PNGs or Cargo.toml changed.\n- **Headless screenshots:** the Open drop-down shows two entries, one greyed \"(missing)\", then Clear recent and Browse….\n\n**Not exercised:** the contributor trying it in a fresh build.\n\nChangelog: Recent projects and models: the Open and Model buttons list the last 10 files opened, saved or imported (newest first, missing files greyed and refused by name, Clear recent, Browse…), kept per user in the config folder (#662)\n\nFixes #662\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAgjpiZbXSvmXLvdmL\n",
